    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d901">

                <pb facs="0811" n="639" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg639"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 855.48/457</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Langhorne</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-14T13:00:00+00:19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 14, 1917, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 2 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>716. Whitlock sends following message by
                    courier:</p>
                <p>Negotiations regarding the relief, the status of Commission for Relief in
                    Belgium, and my position are proceeding. I hope to send a report by next
                    courier. Will the Department in the meantime take no final action in regard to
                        Herter’s telegram sent from Berne?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Langhorne</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
